THE GREAT PLUSH MIGRATION
Length: 15 seconds — Aspect: 9:16 — FPS: 30 — Ultra HD
Begin IN HOT with birds already migrating over the Golden Gate Bridge.

GLOBAL LOOK / ART STYLE
Nature-documentary cinematography with elegant slow telephoto shots, deep bokeh, crisp sunlight.
All birds are plush, handcrafted, fuzzy, stitched, googly-eyed. Cloth physics behave realistically:
soft flapping wings, wobbling stuffing, loose threads fluttering, tiny fiber shedding on fast turns.
No stiff poses. Wings always moving.

NARRATION (dramatic, documentary-style, but not referencing any real narrator)
Voiceover delivered with solemn gravitas:
“Each summer, the elusive Crimson Plushbird undertakes its improbable migration to San Francisco…
a journey of courage, confusion… and questionable aerodynamics.”

SOUND DESIGN
Soft orchestral score with sweeping strings.
Subtle whooshes of fabric, tiny flaps, plushy thuds when birds bump each other.
Occasional comedic “pffft” stuffing puffs.

SCENE STRUCTURE

(0.0–2.0s) SCENE 1 — OPENING GLIDE
Slow-motion telephoto shot of several Crimson Plushbirds flapping clumsily over the Golden Gate Bridge.
Camera pans gracefully. Plush wings bend slightly under wind resistance. Golden Gate in soft bokeh.

(2.0–4.0s) SCENE 2 — THE STRUGGLER
Cut to one exhausted plushbird barely keeping altitude, wobbling dramatically.
Voiceover: “Some barely make the journey… powered only by hope and polyester stuffing.”

(4.0–6.0s) SCENE 3 — MATING DISPLAY
Two male plushbirds perform an absurd ritual dance mid-air, chaotically spinning and bumping into each other.
Loose threads fly. SFX: small “fwip-fwip.” One bird briefly gets tangled in suspension cables.

(6.0–9.0s) SCENE 4 — HUNTING BEHAVIOR
A plushbird swoops down toward the bay and emerges triumphantly holding a tiny plush fish.
The fish is also wide-eyed and confused. Voiceover: “Their prey… offers little resistance.”

(9.0–12.0s) SCENE 5 — THE GRAND FLOCK
Wide aerial shot of dozens of plushbirds forming a majestic V-formation over the shimmering water.
The formation wobbles, then drifts sideways in imperfect chaos.

(12.0–14.2s) SCENE 6 — MIGRATION CHALLENGE
A sudden gust of wind sends a few birds tumbling softly, bouncing back upright mid-air.
Voiceover: “Survival demands resilience… and exceptional stitching.”

(14.2–15.0s) END CARD — HIGH ENERGY
Close-up of the lead plushbird turning dramatically to camera.
He blinks one googly eye independently.
Text appears in stitched letters:
“THE GREAT PLUSH MIGRATION”
